  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pacific Police Development Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Attorney-General&apos;s Department&apos;s (AGD) contribution to the Pacific Police Development Program aims to modernise Pacific island countries&apos; policing, law enforcement and criminal justice legislation and policies. This allows police and justice agencies to respond more effectively to law and justice issues, including violence against women, corruption and transnational crime. AGD works with Pacific island countries and the Australian Federal Police to develop and implement key components of an improved criminal justice system, both bilaterally and regionally. This includes delivery of the Pacific Legal Policy Champions and Pacific Legal Policy Twinning Programs.</narrative>
  </description>
